# Pulled/derived FAAB-pool data - large (combined-training-table.json alone
# is ~436MB, over GitHub's 100MB per-file push limit outright) and the three
# raw pulled-data files can't be regenerated if lost (real bid/roster history
# scraped from other people's public ESPN leagues at a point in time). Not
# in git; instead they're release assets on the "faab-data" GitHub release -
# `python -m tools.faab_history.fetch_release_data` pulls what a normal
# pipeline run needs, `--all` also gets the raw inputs to rebuild the
# training table from scratch via build_training_table.py.
tools/faab_history/combined-training-table.json
tools/faab_history/other-leagues-bids-raw.json
tools/faab_history/other-leagues-bids.json
tools/faab_history/other-leagues-rostered-by-week.json
*.bak

